  "body": "From Tor2web mailing list, by Tom Ritter.\n\nCRIME exploits compression, not a particular cipher.  Somewhere in [0]\nyou need to disable compression.  The relevant option for OpenSSL is\nSSL_OP_NO_COMPRESSION.  In theory you'd add\nctx.set_options(SSL.SSL_OP_NO_COMPRESSION), but in practice, pyOpenSSL\nmay not define that option.\n\n-tom\n\n[0] https://github.com/globaleaks/Tor2web-3.0/blob/master/tor2web/utils/ssl.py#L60\n",
